{"name":"Heidelberg Red","hex":"#960117","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heidelberg","blocks":[{"text":"Heidelberg is the fifth-largest city in the German state of Baden-Württemberg, and with a population of about 163,000, of which roughly a quarter consists of students, it is Germany's 51st-largest city. Located about 78 km (48 mi) south of Frankfurt, Heidelberg is part of the densely populated Rhine-Neckar Metropolitan Region which has its centre in Mannheim."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/K%C3%B6nigstuhl%2C_Heidelberg%2C_U-17.jpg/330px-K%C3%B6nigstuhl%2C_Heidelberg%2C_U-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidelberg","wikidata":"Q2966"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Baden-W%C3%BCrttemberg_Heidelberg_Heiliggeistkirche_01.jpg/500px-Baden-W%C3%BCrttemberg_Heidelberg_Heiliggeistkirche_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Baden-W%C3%BCrttemberg_Heidelberg_Heiliggeistkirche_01.jpg/500px-Baden-W%C3%BCrttemberg_Heidelberg_Heiliggeistkirche_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaden-W%C3%BCrttemberg_Heidelberg_Heiliggeistkirche_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Schloss_Heidelberg_vom_Karlsplatz_gesehen.jpg/500px-Schloss_Heidelberg_vom_Karlsplatz_gesehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Schloss_Heidelberg_vom_Karlsplatz_gesehen.jpg/500px-Schloss_Heidelberg_vom_Karlsplatz_gesehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchloss_Heidelberg_vom_Karlsplatz_gesehen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universit%C3%A4t_v_S%2C_5.jpeg/500px-Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universit%C3%A4t_v_S%2C_5.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universit%C3%A4t_v_S%2C_5.jpeg/1280px-Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universit%C3%A4t_v_S%2C_5.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universit%C3%A4t_v_S%2C_5.jpeg/500px-Heidelberg%2C_Alte_Universi